			<div class="content" id="post-content-4817604">
									

<p><strong>seeking greenlight</strong>: yes</p>
<p><strong>page type</strong>: scp article and experiment logs</p>
<p><strong>elevator pitch</strong>:<br />
-the scp is just the keychain, although the -2 version of it is the entirety of the element oganesson<br />
-the keychain itself isnt much of something special, it just disappears when youre far away from it and reappears when youre too close, depending on your eyesight, and glasses dont affect it<br />
-scp-xxxx-2, oganesson, but when put onto any object, it will have a uniform effect on it, depending on what it is. for example if put onto any keychain it will give it the &quot;draw distance&quot; effect, but if put on say a book itll make it isometric so its size doesnt appear to change no matter how far or close you get to it.<br />
-there can be experiment logs where people can write down a idea for it, and if its good it gets added to the &quot;official&quot; experiment logs, similar to 914.<br />
-original creator has previous test logs used as examples for inspiration.<br />
-different forms of the element have different effects, such as putting something in a box made out of it is different change than dunking it in its liquid form.</p>
<p><strong>central narrative</strong>: after a college student with really poor eye sight tosses his keys to a friend, he notices how a brown part of it disappears, after further experimentation realizes what is happening and posts about it on social media, the foundation finds out about it and confiscates it, and goes on a manhunt to find how it was created, they find a underground meth lab in mexico is responsible for the anomaly, as they find the corpse of someone who shot themselves in the head next to security cameras. searching the lab they find a tank of oganesson gas, and in a closet they also find a journal detailing the experiments done on different substances, including using it to make an essentially endless supply of different illegal substances. after they confiscate all following supply of the element, mostly do to its extremely rare nature, they develop experiment logs similar to those found in 914.</p>
<p><strong>hook</strong>: the keychain itself is just a keychain that disappears with distance, the interesting part is all of the different effects that the xxxx-2 causes on different objects and the test logs, similar to 914 test logs.</p>
<p><strong>notes</strong>: had an idea for a rewrite of the concept and decided to go through with it, i think itd turn out much more interesting than the previous idea. i would also add more examples to the experiment logs but for the sake of brevity ill just leave it to the draft.</p>

