<p>Responding to <a href="/chat-guide">IRC chat</a> request.</p>
<hr />
<p>Quick thing:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>element 118</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like you could have just said &quot;Oganesson&quot; with a quick specification that it is periodic element 118. Despite that, if it's an anomalous gas, I feel like specifying what kind of gas almost defeats the purpose? Just a nitpick, but I figured I'd bring that up anyhow.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>As for the rest of the concept, I'm kind of &quot;meh&quot; on it. I understand the narrative here is meant to get it into the hands of the Foundation, so that's not necessarily a bad start, even if isn't the most exciting thing. It's a good segue into an experiment log, for sure.</p>
<p>However, I'm finding that the lack of specifics on the experiment log is a bit disappointing. I can imagine there are some goofy things that can be done with a perception altering gas, so when there isn't a massive dire consequence or unfortunate accident coupled or mentioned, it's a bit of a let down. There's not a lot for me to comment on with regards to it. Whether that's a fault of the pitch format or not, I can't really say.</p>
<p>I think what could be done here is a total rework of the story here. It might not be the most interesting thing if the Foundation is the one conducting tests with it. However, it might be more interesting to delve into what the person handling this gas has been doing with it. Could be that they discovered the element and conducted their own experimentation with it, only for it to go wrong in a way that one might not expect. Maybe they can't be found because they've become isometric themselves or a chamber holding it sprung a leak and changed the entire room. Think about what other avenues you could explore with regards to how the anomaly is discovered.</p>
</div>
</div>
